{"id":"surface:range-habitat-desert-cottontail-2.0.0","speciesId":"species:desert-cottontail","metric":"HABITAT_SUITABILITY_IN_RANGE","unit":"habitat class inside the supported range","sitesSurveyed":87,"sitesDetected":87,"source":{"authority":"North Ground (range and habitat profile)","title":"Desert cottontail: habitat opportunity inside its range, methodology 2.0.0","url":"https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/search?taxon_key=2436910&country=ca&country=us&license=cc0_1_0&license=cc_by_4_0&hascoordinate=true&hasgeospatialissue=false&occurrencestatus=present&year=2000,2026&basisofrecord=human_observation&basisofrecord=preserved_specimen&basisofrecord=material_sample&basisofrecord=machine_observation&basisofrecord=observation","licence":"North Ground surface; inputs under CC BY 4.0 (Copernicus land cover), CC0 1.0 and CC BY 4.0 (occurrence records through GBIF.org) and the public domain (NOAA ETOPO 2022)","attribution":"Contains modified Copernicus Global Land Service information (2019). Buchhorn, M. et al., Copernicus Global Land Service: Land Cover 100m: collection 3: epoch 2019: Globe. Range from occurrence records published through GBIF.org (retrieved 2026-09-30) by the 27 datasets credited in content/intelligence/range-habitat/datasets.json. NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information. 2022: ETOPO 2022 15 Arc-Second Global Relief Model. doi:10.25921/fd45-gt74.","retrievedAt":"2026-09-30","verifiedAt":"2026-09-30"},"limitations":["How well the land suits desert cottontail, inside the range records place it. Habitat, not a count of animals and not a density.","The range is ground within 25 km of places where openly licensed records confirm the species; where people rarely record wildlife, real range can be missing, and records can be wrong.","Records decide only whether ground is in the range; they never set a cell's colour, so where more people report wildlife does not become where there are more animals. Small mammals are recorded where people walk and look;